<title>USA: Beverly says court stays reinstatement order.</title>
<headline>Beverly says court stays reinstatement order.</headline>
<dateline>CHAMBERSBURG, Pa. 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beverly Enterprises Inc said Thursday a federal judge has granted a stay of an injunction that the company reinstate workers in Pennsylvania who went on strike in April.</p>
<p>Beverly said the National Labor Relations Board, which had sought the injunction in the case on behalf of the Service Employees Union, consented to the stay.</p>
<p>The injunction was granted January 21 by Judge D. Brooks Smith and he granted Beverly Enteprise's request for a stay January 29, the company said.   The company said that since the</p>
<p>strike, it has rehired all but 68 of the strikers.</p>
</text>
